{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_flags` in `repo/cli.py`, so `--key=value` is now split into a key and a value. `parse_flags([\"--out=log.txt\"])` returns `{\"out\": \"log.txt\"}`, and both visible tests pass.\n\nWhen a flag contains `=`, the function now splits it at the first `=` and stores that value straight away. It doesn't look at the next argument in that case. Splitting only at the first `=` means values that contain `=` stay whole: `--q=a=b` gives `{\"q\": \"a=b\"}`. An empty value also works: `--x=` gives `{\"x\": \"\"}`. The `--flag` form (stored as `True`) and the `--key value` form behave as before. I also removed the old `BUG` comment."}]},"session_id":"ab667c0c-c58e-423e-b00a-5ea108d4d59f"}
